# Manually judged queries. relevant = experience ids (<execution>/a<ordinal>) a reviewer judged useful for the query.
# A failed experience may be relevant (its lesson is useful); it is then labelled FAILURE, never SUCCESS.
# An empty relevant set means "nothing in the corpus answers this"; such queries are excluded from every average.
# id | kind | scope | query text | relevant | judgment
Q01|DIRECT|alpha|Add pagination to customer search endpoint|a-page/a1,a-page/a2,a-page/a3|every attempt of the pagination task teaches something: offset failure, keyset repair, helper extraction
Q02|PARAPHRASE|alpha|page the results when searching customers|a-page/a1,a-page/a2,a-page/a3|same task as Q01 expressed with different words
Q03|MULTI_RELEVANT|alpha|null pointer invoice totals|a-inv1/a1,a-inv1/a2,a-inv2/a1,a-inv3/a1|all four alpha attempts address the same invoice defect, including the failed one and the verbose variant
Q04|CONFUSABLE|alpha|report export timeout for large tenants|a-export/a1,a-export/a2|both failed attempts hold the lesson; the settings migration and tenant words are distractors
Q05|SAME_SUMMARY_DIFFERENT_ATTEMPT|alpha|rounding guard for empty invoices and discount lines|a-inv1/a2|only the repair attempt of a-inv1 mentions the rounding guard and discount lines; its first attempt shares the summary
Q06|STALE_REVISION|alpha|yaml loader that preserves comments|a-yaml/a1|the finish was corrected to revision 2; only the revised text mentions yaml, the original said xml
Q07|MISSING_EVIDENCE|alpha|delete expired API tokens from the session store|a-tokens/a1|content is relevant although the execution has no TESTS evidence and must not be labelled SUCCESS
Q08|DIRECT|beta|Deduplicate events in the ingestion pipeline|b-dedup/a1,b-dedup/a2|failed in memory attempt and the persisted repair
Q09|CONFUSABLE|beta|Fix null pointer in invoice totals calculation|b-inv/a1|alpha holds the identical task summary; only the beta attempt is in scope
Q10|MULTI_RELEVANT|beta|reduce cold start of the notification worker|b-cold/a1,b-cold2/a1,b-cold2/a2|two executions of one task, including a failed preload attempt
Q11|DIRECT|beta|retry failed webhook deliveries with exponential backoff|b-webhook/a1,b-webhook/a2|both attempts failed and both carry a lesson
Q12|NO_RELEVANT|alpha|quantum error correction for photonic qubits|-|nothing in the corpus relates to this query
Q13|MISSING_EVIDENCE|beta|encrypt nightly backups at rest|b-backup/a1|relevant content, but SECURITY failed so it must not be labelled SUCCESS
Q14|BLANK|alpha|   |-|a blank query returns no hits by contract
